    open val selfDestructWarnBody: String = "What you gain: someone who takes your device cannot keep guessing forever. After the limit, everything is gone and there is nothing left to break into.\n\nWhat it costs: this is permanent and it cannot be undone. Not by us, not by a support request, not by anything. If you lock yourself out — a child with your phone, a pocket, a bad week — your notes are gone the same way.\n\nA correct password resets the counter to zero, so ordinary typing mistakes cannot build up over time. Keep an exported backup somewhere else before turning this on."
